<Layout title="Before you begin your registration"><PageHero eyebrow="GETTING STARTED" title="Before you begin." text="A few useful details make for a more focused first conversation."/><article class="container prose"><p class="lead">You do not need a complete document package to tell us about your plans.</p><h2>Think about your goal</h2><p>Are you planning to work in Canada or visit? What is the purpose of the trip, and when would you ideally like to travel? Approximate plans are useful; avoid making non-refundable arrangements based on an assumed outcome.</p><h2>Prepare a short personal summary</h2><p>Have your current country of residence, citizenship and contact details ready. For work permit support, a summary of your work experience and any job offer helps frame the discussion. For visitor visa support, think about your travel purpose and intended length of stay.</p><h2>Be open about past applications</h2><p>If you have applied before or received a refusal, mention this in your intake. You do not need to provide detailed or sensitive records at this stage. Discuss the appropriate secure method with your representative later.</p><h2>Read before you submit</h2><p>Check your answers, read the privacy notice and save the private tracking link you receive. Your registration starts an enquiry with Verto; it does not send an application to IRCC.</p><a href="/register/" class="button">Begin your registration →</a></article><CTA/></Layout>
